{
  "component": "Checkbox Field",
  "description": "A checkbox with a label, an optional description line and an optional error line. Five states and three value types combine into fifteen variants. PURPOSE: Lets people turn a single option on or off, or show a mixed selection, with supporting text underneath when the choice needs explaining and an error line when the input fails validation. BEHAVIOUR: State controls the visual treatment across Default, Hover, Focus, Disabled and Error. Focus applies Border/Focus/Default with Stroke/Focus Ring. Hover swaps the box fill to Background/Brand/Hover when selected and Background/Default/Default Hover when empty. Error applies Border/Danger/Default to the box and Text/Danger/Default to the error line. Value Type switches the box between empty, a Check glyph and a Minus glyph, with Background/Brand/Default filling the box when selected or indeterminate. Disabled variants use Background/Disabled/Default, Border/Disabled/default, Icon/Disabled/On Disabled and Text/Disabled/Default. COMPOSITION: Each variant holds a Checkbox and Label row (the Checkbox frame with its glyph, plus a Label text layer), a Description Row and an Error Row, each made of a Space spacer and a text layer that aligns the text under the label. The Check and Minus icon instances are nested components. Code generators should look for existing Check and Minus icon components in the codebase before building new ones. USAGE: Use for independent on/off choices and for parent rows in a nested list, where Indeterminate signals that only some children are selected. Use a radio group when options are mutually exclusive, and a switch when the change applies immediately. Turn Has Description off when the label is self-explanatory, and turn Has Error on only while the field is invalid. CODE GENERATION NOTES: Render as an input of type checkbox with a real label element rather than a styled div. Indeterminate cannot be set in HTML markup, so set the DOM property in script. Hover, Focus and Error are visual states and should come from CSS pseudo-classes and validation state, not variant props. Link the description and the error text with aria-describedby and set aria-invalid when the error is shown. Disabled variants should set the disabled attribute so clicks and focus are blocked, and the whole row including the label should be clickable.",
