  "namingIssues": null,
  "existingDescription": "A checkbox with a label and an optional description line, published as 12 variants covering four states and three value types. PURPOSE: Lets people turn a single option on or off, or show a mixed selection, with supporting text underneath when the choice needs explaining. BEHAVIOUR: State controls the visual treatment across Default, Hover, Focus and Disabled. Focus applies the Border/Focus/Default colour with Stroke/Focus Ring. Value Type switches the box between empty, a Check glyph and a Minus glyph, with Background/Brand/Default filling the box when selected or indeterminate. Disabled variants swap to Background/Disabled/Default, Border/Disabled/default and Icon/Disabled/On Disabled. COMPOSITION: Each variant holds a Checkbox and Label row (the Checkbox frame with its glyph, plus a Label text layer) and a Description Row (a Space spacer plus a Description text layer). The Check and Minus icon instances are nested components. Code generators should look for existing Check and Minus icon components in the codebase before building new ones. USAGE: Use for independent on/off choices and for parent rows in a nested list, where Indeterminate signals that only some children are selected. Use a radio group when options are mutually exclusive, and a switch when the change applies immediately. Turn Has Description off when the label is self-explanatory. CODE GENERATION NOTES: Render as an input of type checkbox with a real label element rather than a styled div. Indeterminate cannot be set in HTML markup, so set the DOM property in script. Hover and Focus are visual states and should come from CSS pseudo-classes, not variant props. Link the description with aria-describedby. Disabled variants should set the disabled attribute so clicks and focus are blocked, and the whole row including the label should be clickable.",
